-- title:
--   Unimodularity of GL₃ over the adeles of ℚ
-- statement:
--   Write $\mathbb{A}$ for the adele ring $\mathrm{AdeleRing}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}},\mathbb{Q})$ of the rationals and let $G = GL_3(\mathbb{A})$ be the general linear group of $3\times 3$ matrices over $\mathbb{A}$, indexed by `Fin 3`, equipped with the Borel $\sigma$-algebra `glBorel` generated by its topology. On $G$ the measure `adelicGLHaar (Fin 3) (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ` is Mathlib's canonical left Haar measure `Measure.haar` for this Borel structure. The theorem asserts that this measure is in addition right invariant: for every $h \in G$ the pushforward of the measure along right translation $g \mapsto gh$ equals the measure itself, so that $\mu(Eh) = \mu(E)$ for every Borel set $E \subseteq G$. Equivalently, $GL_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ is unimodular, its left Haar measure being also a right Haar measure. The proof invokes second countability of the adele ring of a number field, [`NumberField.AdeleRing.secondCountableTopology`](thm.html#NumberField.AdeleRing.secondCountableTopology).
--
--   This is the unimodularity of $GL_3$ over the adeles of $\mathbb{Q}$, the rank three analogue over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the corresponding statement for $GL_2$ over a number field; left invariance is built into the measure, while right invariance amounts to triviality of the modular character. It is used in the cubic induction step of the Langlands–Tunnell argument, where right translation of functions on $GL_3(\mathbb{A})$ must preserve $L^2$ norms and cuspidality conditions.
